  "question": {
    "text": "Homoleptic octahedral complexes of a metal ion <math><mi>&#8242;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mi>&#8242;</mi></math> with three monodentate ligands <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> absorb wavelengths in the region of green, blue and red respectively. The increasing order of the ligand strength is:",
