  "solution": {
    "text": "Observed order of wavelengths,&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></math> <math><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>.<br /><br />(Red light has highest wavelength of 700 nm while blue is the shortest with a wavelength of about 480 nm)<br /><br />So,&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> (strength of ligands) order&nbsp; will be <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>.<br /><br />(As <math><msub><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0&#160;</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#945;&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> )<br /><br />Hence, order will be <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>.<br /><br />Therefore, Strength of ligand <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub></math>.",
